{pause down}
# A pattern I keep seeing

{pause}
Twenty years ago: explaining strong typing to dynamic-language
programmers. {pause} Ten years ago: explaining gradual types to PHP
programmers at Facebook — they're all convinced now. {pause}

{.remark pause}
Today: explaining capability types to OCaml programmers. Same
reaction. Some very smart people are still against it.

{pause}
{.block title="A twist"}
The original "reasoning is easier" argument was never the killer one —
**maintenance and refactoring** were. {pause} For capability types, the
new killer argument is **reviewing AI-generated code**.
